  <div class="legal">
    <h1>About Learn with me</h1>
    <p class="muted">A private, searchable learning library for Guidewire and Gosu developers.</p>

    <p>Learn with me is a curated library that makes it easy to browse, search, and copy practical Guidewire Gosu query files. Content is organized as a topic hierarchy mirrored from the server’s <code>queries/</code> directory, so new topics appear automatically when folders and files are added.</p>

    <h2>What you’ll find</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Guidewire Gosu queries and logic examples (PC, BC, CC) for everyday development tasks.</li>
      <li>Tutorial videos and walkthroughs where available.</li>
      <li>Reference material and downloadable resources that remain separate from ad-eligible learning content.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Sign in with Google — new accounts are pending until an administrator approves access for a limited period.</li>
      <li>Browse folders or search the library; open a query to view the code, copy it, like it, and ask questions.</li>
      <li>Discussions are attached to each content item so you can ask and answer in context.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it’s for</h2>
    <p>Developers, analysts, and learners working with Guidewire and related technologies who want practical, searchable examples without hunting through scattered files.</p>

    <h2>Contact & Support</h2>
    <p>For access requests, content questions, or to report an issue, contact the library administrator:</p>
    <p><a href="mailto:learnwithmegw@gmail.com">learnwithmegw@gmail.com</a> — also listed in the site footer on every page.</p>
    <p class="muted">Future public launch will keep PDFs, restricted reference materials, and any restricted/private content separate from advertising. See our <a href="/content-policy">Content &amp; Copyright Policy</a> for details.</p>
  </div>
</main>
